Title:
Dark Agent (Mythic C2 Agent for Linux/macOS with in-memory BOF loader)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Dark Agent is a production-ready Mythic C2 agent targeting Linux and macOS, implemented in Crystal with a focus on post-exploitation tradecraft and extensibility. It provides an in-memory COFF/BOF loader and a large set of built-in and BOF-backed Unix-style commands (process, file, network, and system enumeration/manipulation). The project includes HTTP and a malleable “HTTPX” C2 profile supporting domain rotation, traffic transforms, and flexible message placement (headers/params/cookies/body). It emphasizes deployment practicality via statically linked OpenSSL on Linux (no libssl dependency) and cross-compiled macOS arm64 builds with ad-hoc signing requirements for newer macOS versions. Operational safety controls are built in (operator approvals for risky actions like shell, low sleep, and kill). Useful primarily for red teams/pentesters using Mythic who need a mature Unix agent with BOF ecosystem support and configurable network evasion.

Technical Focus:
- Mythic agent development (payload type, commands, browser scripts integration)
- In-memory COFF/BOF loading and execution (Beacon-style APIs)
- Malleable HTTP C2 (domain rotation, transforms, message placement)
- Static OpenSSL linking and cross-compilation (Zig, rcodesign) for macOS/Linux
- SOCKS5 proxying and chunked file transfer mechanisms

Use Cases:
- Deploy a Linux/macOS Mythic implant with configurable HTTP/HTTPX communications
- Run post-exploitation tasks via BOFs without dropping tooling to disk
- Develop/test custom BOFs using “direct mode” standalone COFF loader
- Establish SOCKS5 pivoting through compromised Unix hosts
- Perform host/network discovery and basic anti-forensics (e.g., timestomp) via BOF commands

Keywords:
Mythic C2, Dark Agent, Crystal, Linux implant, macOS arm64, COFF, BOF, Beacon API, in-memory execution, HTTP C2, malleable C2, HTTPX profile, domain rotation, traffic transforms, AES-256-CBC, OpenSSL static linking, SOCKS5 proxy, Zig cross-compile, rcodesign, chunked file transfer